  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 504.07 Service Line and Water Meter Installation and Maintenance Policy",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 504.07 Service Line and Water Meter Installation and Maintenance Policy.\n\n(a) Unless the PWS has adopted formal rules to the contrary, the service line and service meter policy shall be as follows:\n\n(1) The owner of a PWS shall be responsible for the service line from the water main to the curb stop;\n\n(2) The service customer shall be responsible for the service line from the curb stop to the customer’s premises; and\n\n(3) The owner of a PWS shall be responsible for any required service meters.\n\n(b) The owner of a PWS shall select, size, install, and maintain all required water meters in accordance with:\n\n(1) The specifications of the manufacturer; and\n\n(2) The procedures and protocols described in “Manual of Water Supply Practices, Water Meters – Selection, Installation, Testing, and Maintenance,” document identification number AWWA M6, American Water Works Association, 2012, available as noted in Appendix C.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 504) #10465, eff 12-2-13; ss by #14006, eff 6-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw500.html"
